  "description": "A modal jazz-funk groove in D Dorian at 116 bpm: the mode, not a minor key, is the colour. The vamp is Dm9 to G13, the major IV that only Dorian has (its B natural, the raised 6th), and the bridge moves the whole vamp a half step up (Ebm9 Ab13, Eb Dorian), the move of modal jazz. A drawbar organ comps in short off-beat stabs through a chorus for the rotary speaker, held chords in the intro. The bass is a two-bar ostinato written as notes that walks through the 6th (B over Dm9, C over Ebm9). The sampled kit plays a jazz-funk groove with a light sixteenth swing: a kick that avoids the beats after the 1, a snare on 2 and 4 with ghost notes between, sixteenth hats, the ride in the bridge, a fill at every eighth bar. The lead melody leans on the 6th (B natural, then C in the bridge) and changes its last phrase on the return; the outro drops to the ride and the organ.",
